          "notes": [
            {
              "chapter": 30,
              "v_start": 5,
              "v_end": 5,
              "text": "Cometh — Speedily and in due season."
            },
            {
              "chapter": 30,
              "v_start": 7,
              "v_end": 7,
              "text": "Mountain — My kingdom: kingdoms are usually called mountains in prophetical writings."
            },
            {
              "chapter": 30,
              "v_start": 9,
              "v_end": 9,
              "text": "Profit — What wilt thou gain by it? The dust - Shall they that are dead celebrate thy goodness in the land of the living? Or, shall my dust praise thee?"
            },
            {
              "chapter": 30,
              "v_start": 11,
              "v_end": 11,
              "text": "Sackcloth — Given me occasion to put off that sackcloth, which they used to wear in times of mourning, Esth iv, 1 chap. xxxv, 13 Isaiah xxxii, 11 Joel i, 13. Girded - With joy, as with a garment, surrounding me on every side."
            },
            {
              "chapter": 30,
              "v_start": 12,
              "v_end": 12,
              "text": "My glory — My tongue. David professes his confidence in God, intermixing prayer to him, ver. 1-8. Complains to God and prays for deliverance, ver. 9-18. Concludes with giving glory to God, and encouraging others to trust him, ver. 19-24. To the chief musician, A psalm of David."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "role": "second",
          "ref": "2 Corinthians 8:7-15",
          "refKey": "2Cor.8.7-2Cor.8.15",
